Step 1 - Create Spring Boot Project

In Spring Initializr choose
Project : Maven
Language : Java
Spring Boot : 3.5.17
Java : 17
--> Dependencies used :
Spring Web
Spring Data JPA
MySQL Driver
Validation
Lombok (optional)

--> Click Generate.
--> Open in STS.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 2 - Configure Database

Create database :
CREATE DATABASE ecommerce_db;
Inside application.properties
write :
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/ecommerce_db
spring.datasource.username=root
spring.datasource.password=Root
spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
spring.jpa.show-sql=true

Now Spring knows where to store data.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 3 - Create Packages

Create these packages :
controller
entity
repository
service
serviceimpl
--> This is the project skeleton.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 4 - Create Entity Classes

Now create database tables.
Each class becomes one table.

Customer
Product
ShoppingCart
CartItem
Order
OrderItem
Payment
Each entity contains :
@Id
@GeneratedValue
@Column
-- > When application starts, Hibernate automatically creates table.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 5 - Create Repository
--> Repository talks to MySQL.

Example :
public interface ProductRepository
extends JpaRepository<Product, Long>{}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 6 - Create Service Interface
Service contains business methods.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 7 - Create Service Implementation

--> Now write actual logic.
--> Inject repository
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 8 - Create Controller
--> Controller receives HTTP requests.
Example :
POST
GET
PUT
DELETE
--> Controller calls Service.
--> Service calls Repository.
--> Repository talks to Database.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 9 - Run Project
Run --> EcommerceApiApplication.java
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
